From 0fef47d167f29e3619af309ca897ba9efa7d434c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:37:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] l2r-local: entry 23-e: worklist drops: nullable members
 and locked cells

Fourth step: worklist glue (23-d) defers every box of its record's cycle
itself, so that nesting stays bounded by the type graph. Two ways
remained in which glue released such a box through the record's entry,
one native frame per level of the value (a chain linked through a
nullable member overflowed a 256 KiB stack in
runtime/drop_member_order.mlir's chains with worklist-drops on):

- A nullable member's non-null box of a Worklist record is now deferred
  like a plain member box.
- A locked cell's payload is released, inside its critical section, by
  a `__reussir_locked_drop` function, now under every option, not only
  under retcon-drops. Released inline in the critical section, the
  payload's decrement token was never freed: frontend/retcon_drop.rr
  leaked the Arc box held by a Mutex<Arc<Tree>> under ASan, and so does
  TPDE mode on l2r-base7 (neither option set; a 24-byte ASan leak). Inside
  glue the function is a separate one, `__reussir_locked_drop.worklist`,
  marked as glue, so that it defers the payload's Worklist box; outside
  glue the ordinary one, which drops the payload through its entry.

Boxes in record members, arrays and unlocked cells were already deferred
by 23-d (the walk expands them inline). A record reached through another
record's box is not affected: that box's own drop runs its own glue, or,
outside the cycle, is bounded by the type graph.

Tests: conversion/worklist_drop_members.mlir (a record linked to itself
through a nullable, a cell, a mutex cell and a plain member: four
deferrals, one in the glue locked drop, no tail release helper; a mutex
cell dropped outside glue uses the ordinary locked drop);
conversion/locked_cell_drop.mlir (TPDE's options: the locked drop frees
its token); conversion/retcon_drop.mlir's run without retcon drops no
longer excludes `__reussir_locked_drop`; conversion/mutex_cell_drop,
rwlock_cell_drop and flatlock_cell_drop.mlir check the critical section's
call of the locked drop and, in the locked drop, the payload's decrement
(and the inner box's free, now under the lock).
